nodecode-live-time is a rewrite of chenfeijiang95-ui's chenfeijiang95-ui/hermes-live-time:

  https://github.com/chenfeijiang95-ui/hermes-live-time
  commit f5e4edcefb19f68f11c0e3faf5f6983577500c75
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 chenfeijiang95-ui (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the whole reading -- the timezone-aware clock, the weekday, the UTC
offset and the block's wording, which claims authority over "now" and calls an
earlier session-start stamp history; the timezone resolution (the plugin's
hermes_time resolver and its config.yaml timezone key became the cell's
timezone setting, read from the tz database instead of through the host
runtime); the fail-open posture, so an unreadable zone costs the machine's own
zone rather than the turn; and the section itself, which is the cell's config
section.

Left out: the hook's placement. The plugin injected its block into the user
message of every single request through a Hermes-only pre_llm_call hook; a cell
has one standing context seam, the harness section the engine reads at a turn's
first request and freezes for that turn's rounds, so the reading is per turn
here rather than per request. Two things carry the difference: the block names
its own instant, and a current_time tool reads the clock again inside a turn
that runs long. Also left out: hermes_time and hermes_yaml, the runtime
modules the plugin imported for profile routing and YAML parsing, which a cell
does not have; and the plugin's YAML file parsing, replaced by the tz database
under zoneinfo_dir. /time, the current_time tool and the (help :live-time)
topic are additions, not part of the original.
